# Lick: Tapping Arpeggios (repertoire plan: st-lick-tapping). An original 8-bar lick on string 1
# only, in triplet eighths: every beat is tap, pull-off, hammer-on, so each beat is one arpeggio.
#   Am (bars 1-2): tap fret 12 (E), pull off to fret 5 (A), hammer fret 8 (C)
#   F  (bars 3-4): tap fret 13 (F), pull off to fret 5 (A), hammer fret 8 (C)
#   G  (bars 5-6): tap fret 15 (G), pull off to fret 7 (B), hammer fret 10 (D)
#   E  (bars 7-8): tap fret 12 (E), pull off to fret 4 (G#), hammer fret 7 (B)
# The left hand stays a minor third wide (finger 1 and finger 4, three frets apart) and just
# moves the shape; the tapped notes sing a slow tune of their own on top: E, F, G, E. The lick
# ends on a held tap on the high E, the root of E, which leads back to Am when you loop it.
# The teacher strums the chords.
title: Lick: Tapping Arpeggios
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: tapping, legato, arpeggios, one string, triplets
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: Am

